# recovery-exec (Proxmox investigate landing account on {{ inventory_hostname }}):
# fixed privileged read-only cluster / HA / replication / storage / ZFS /
# journal status checks only. The world-readable replication job logs are
# read directly by the dispatch script and need no sudo rule. No pvesh
# create/set/delete. No wildcard arguments anywhere below — each line is the
# complete, fixed privileged command the dispatch script invokes; nothing
# else can match.
#
# On sudo argument matching: sudo compares the command's arguments as a single
# space-joined string (fnmatch), NOT token-by-token. So the journalctl
# `--since "-2 hours"` invocation in the dispatch script (one argv element
# containing a space) matches the unquoted `--since -2 hours` below — the two
# join to the identical string. Do NOT "fix" this by adding double quotes:
# sudoers does not shell-dequote, so a literal `"` here would only match a
# literal `"` in argv and break the match. No wildcard is involved.
#
# NOTE (pre-deploy check): confirm the ha-manager path below with
# `which ha-manager` on this node before/at first deploy — /usr/sbin is the
# standard Proxmox VE location but has not been verified against this host.
#
# NOTE (pre-deploy check): confirm the absolute paths of the new binaries on
# this node match the paths below (they must match EXACTLY for sudoers to
# match): `command -v pvesr pvecm pvesm zpool zfs journalctl`. Expected paths,
# fixed here and in recovery-investigate-dispatch-pve.sh.j2:
#   /usr/bin/pvesr    /usr/bin/pvecm      (pve-manager/pve-cluster, like pvesh)
#   /usr/sbin/pvesm                       (pve-storage; NOT /usr/bin — see below)
#   /usr/sbin/zpool   /usr/sbin/zfs       (zfsutils; may be /sbin on some hosts)
#   /usr/bin/journalctl
# pvesm was corrected /usr/bin -> /usr/sbin after review F3 (2026-07-14_005):
# Proxmox VE ships pvesm in /usr/sbin, so the earlier "all pve CLIs in /usr/bin"
# assumption was wrong for pvesm. If tester's `command -v` finds any other
# path, update the matching line here and in the dispatch script.
#
# NOTE (pre-deploy check): confirm the remaining journalctl target units below
# exist on this node (`systemctl list-units --all 'pve-cluster*' 'corosync*'
# 'pvedaemon*'`). journalctl with `-u <nonexistent>` still exits 0 (empty
# output), so a wrong/removed unit fails silently rather than erroring.
#
# NOTE (pre-deploy check): forced command + no-pty means sudo runs with no
# controlling tty. Confirm `sudo -n` succeeds here (this Proxmox/Debian host
# may set `Defaults requiretty` unlike authy/monnie's Ubuntu default) —
# verify with the cluster-status check first, before trusting the rest.
recovery-exec ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/pvesh get /cluster/status --output-format json
recovery-exec ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/pvesh get /cluster/resources --output-format json
recovery-exec ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/ha-manager status
recovery-exec ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/pvesr status
recovery-exec ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/pvesr list
recovery-exec ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/pvecm status
recovery-exec ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/pvesm status
recovery-exec ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/zpool status -x
recovery-exec ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/zfs list
recovery-exec ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/journalctl -p warning..err --since -2 hours -n 300 --no-pager
recovery-exec ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/journalctl -u pve-cluster -u corosync -u pvedaemon --since -2 hours -n 200 --no-pager
